THIRD-PARTY LICENSES — @mnmal-ai/holomap-clusterer
==================================================

Why this file exists
--------------------

`wasm/holomap_clusterer_bg.wasm` is a *combined work*. It is the Rust crate
`holomap-clusterer` compiled to `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with all of its Rust
dependencies statically linked in — there is no dynamic linking and no
separate artifact for them. Distributing this npm package therefore
distributes compiled forms of every crate listed below, and their license
terms travel with it.

The Rust crate has never been in this position: crates.io ships source, and
the consumer's own `cargo build` resolves and links dependencies under their
own terms. This npm package is the first distribution of the combined binary,
so it is the first that owes attribution for the linked code.

Three of the linked crates are **Apache-2.0 only** — they offer no MIT
alternative:

    approx    0.5.1    Apache-2.0
    nalgebra  0.35.0   Apache-2.0
    simba     0.10.0   Apache-2.0

`nalgebra` is what `holomap` uses for the pure-Rust eigensolves behind its
spectral initialisation; `simba` and `approx` come in transitively with it.

What this means for you
-----------------------

This package's own code — the TypeScript in `dist/`, the Rust in
`crates/holomap-clusterer/`, and the `holomap` crate — is licensed
**MIT OR Apache-2.0**, at your option. That is unchanged and is what
`package.json` declares.

The three crates above are not dual-licensed, so the Apache-2.0 terms apply to
their contribution to the `.wasm` regardless of which option you take for
ours. Taking Apache-2.0 for the whole artifact is the simplest reading and is
fully consistent — Apache-2.0 is already one of the two options this package
offers. The full text is shipped alongside this file as `LICENSE-APACHE`; the
MIT text is `LICENSE-MIT`.

Apache-2.0 §4(d) — the NOTICE-file obligation — is satisfied vacuously here:
none of `approx` 0.5.1, `nalgebra` 0.35.0 or `simba` 0.10.0 ships a NOTICE
file in its crates.io artifact (each ships only a bare, unmodified copy of the
Apache-2.0 text). There is no NOTICE content to propagate. Verified against
the vendored sources for these exact versions; re-verify if the versions move.

Nothing in `dist/` is affected. The TypeScript sources and the wasm-bindgen
JS glue in `wasm/holomap_clusterer.js` are MIT-or-Apache dual-licensed
throughout; the Apache-only code exists solely inside the `.wasm` binary.


