Build-time only — NOT linked into the .wasm
-------------------------------------------

These are procedural macros and their support crates. They run inside the
compiler and generate source; none of their own code is present in the
shipped binary. Listed for completeness because they appear in the
dependency graph, not because attribution is owed for them.

    bumpalo                    3.20.3    MIT OR Apache-2.0
    proc-macro2                1.0.106   MIT OR Apache-2.0
    quote                      1.0.45    MIT OR Apache-2.0
    serde_derive               1.0.228   MIT OR Apache-2.0
    syn                        2.0.117   MIT OR Apache-2.0
    thiserror-impl             1.0.69    MIT OR Apache-2.0
    unicode-ident              1.0.24    (MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND Unicode-3.0
    wasm-bindgen-macro         0.2.126   MIT OR Apache-2.0
    wasm-bindgen-macro-support 0.2.126   MIT OR Apache-2.0

`unicode-ident` carries a Unicode-3.0 term. It is reachable only through
`proc-macro2`, which is reachable only through proc-macro crates, so its
tables are compiler-side data and not part of the distributed artifact.
It is called out anyway so a future reader who moves it into a shipped
path knows there is a third license family to account for.


Regenerating this list
----------------------

    cargo tree -p holomap-clusterer --features wasm \
      --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -e normal --prefix none --no-dedupe \
      | sort -u

Cross-reference the `license` field from `cargo metadata` for each name. The
build-time/shipped split is determined with `cargo tree -i <crate>`: a crate
reachable *only* beneath a `(proc-macro)` node is build-time only. Note that
`wasm-bindgen-shared` is reachable both ways and therefore ships.

This file is maintained by hand and is accurate as of the dependency versions
pinned in `Cargo.lock`. A dependency bump can change it — re-run the above
whenever `Cargo.lock` moves, and in particular re-check whether any newly
Apache-only crate has entered the graph.
